---

This is a derivative work.

The Autopilot skill — its phases, gates, manifest design and dashboard — was
written by Nick Vels and published at https://github.com/nick-vels/skills
under the MIT licence above. The overwhelming majority of the text in
.github/skills/autopilot/ is his, unchanged.

This package adapts that skill to VS Code with GitHub Copilot agent mode.
What is new here: the four agent definitions in .github/agents/, the
file-backed replacements for stateless subagents, the Windows and PowerShell
adaptations, the VS Code settings, and the documentation in README.md and
FIRST-RUN.md. See "What is different from the Claude Code original" in
README.md for the full list.

Both the original and the port are MIT. Nothing here restricts what upstream
already granted.
